window.products.push({"id":1187527,"name":"AudioSource AMP 210 90-Watt Stereo 250-Watt Mono Power Amplifier (Black)","category":"electronics","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Zp+H2mKTL._AC_.jpg","description":"Product Description AudioSource AMP series amplifiers are designed for home and commercial audio distribution systems where high quality sound, flexibility, and reliability are essential. The AudioSource AMP 210 delivers 90 watts of stereo power at <0.1% THD and 250 watts of mono power at <0.2% THD. All AudioSource amps – AMP 102, AMP 110, AMP 210, and AMP 310 are rack-mount ready, full bandwidth capable, bridgeable for incredible mono power, and feature two zones of output with A/B or A+B speaker selection, providing a repertoire of flexible configurations. They boast a robust power supply and bipolar output devices. Front panel diagnostic LED displays show clipping to prevent over-driving your speakers. With second source override our amps automatically access secondary sources such as MP3 players, satellite radio, PA systems, paging, game consoles, phone calls or even doorbells. Speaker level inputs add another dimension to the usefulness of these fine amps; allowing for installation where only speaker wires are present to carry the signal information. For high power applications, the AMP 210 and AMP 310 are designed so users can set a safe maximum level using the rear panel master level controls, then make fine adjustments on the front panel. All AudioSource amplifiers are easy to install and are torture tested during development to ensure years of use.Trouble shooting steps: - To bring the unit out of protect mode, you must cycle the front panel power button. Protect mode is a typical indication that the amplifier has a speaker load impedance of less than 4 ohms per channel, improperly connected Impedance matching volume controls.- To avoid static noise often check the RCA cable and try replacing it.- To be noted: Orange lights indicate the unit is in thermal protect mode, or is in trigger mode waiting for trigger signal. If in thermal protect mode, the unit may have been used too hard, wired incorrectly, or not properly vented, among other potential causes.- To be checked: Check RCA cables connected to input and use a different input source to determine if they are at fault. Check Rear panel Level Controls to ensure both left and right are set correctly. Check front panel Balance knob to ensure it is set correctly. From the Manufacturer AudioSource AMP-210 Amplifier: Clean Power Meets Ease of Use for Flexible Home Theater Applications AudioSource started designing and building amps over 20 years ago. Over time, AudioSource has continually refined its products to balance power, sound clarity and long-lasting performance. The perfect balance of power, sound clarity and long lasting performance. View larger Like the rest of AudioSource's line of amps, the AMP-210 is full-bandwidth capable, bridgeable, and features A-B switching, providing a repertoire of flexible configurations. It features a robust power supply and bipolar output devices, with source override to accommodate necessary interruptions such as PA systems, game consoles, phone calls, or even doorbells. All AudioSource electronics, including amplifiers, equalizers, volume controls and more, are easy to install and torture-tested during development to ensure years of use. This AudioSource AMP-210 two-channel power amplifier is built to deliver powerful music, pure and simple, with few extra controls to get in the way. Listeners can use the AMP-210 as an independent stereo amp (90 watts x 2 into 8 ohms) when used with a preamp, as a second zone amplifier in multi-room applications, or as a rear-channel amplifier in a 6.1- and 7.1-channel system. Combine the AMP-210 with an additional monoblock amp (the AMP-210 delivers 250 watts RMS of bridged power) and a preamp, and listeners can independently drive two front left/right speakers or two rear speakers, further clarifying each channel to create dynamic high-end sound. To connect additional components to the amp, use the included stereo inputs with automatic priority override (for connecting to a source such as a receiver, CD player, or preamplifier)--or use the auxiliary output for creating a multi-amp setup. The AMP-210 boasts a precise frequency response of 10 Hz to 50 kHz and total harmonic distortion of 0.02 percent. Additional features include A, B, or A+B speaker selector switches, a 12-volt trigger, front-panel mounted volume and balance knobs, stereo speaker level inputs, and five-way binding posts that work with both bare wire and banana plugs. Plus, at 16-1/2 by 3-13/16 by 13-3/4 inches (W x H x D), the device should fit comfortably in most rack mount or home entertainment setups. The AMP-210 works perfectly with AudioSource's AMP2UEAR rack solution. All AudioSource amps are backed by a two-year warranty on parts and labor. Which AudioSource Amplifier is Right for You? Model Watts Per Channel Features at a Glance Stereo8 Ohms Stereo4 Ohms Bridged8 Ohms Channels Inputs PriorityInputSwitching A/BSpeakerSelection Auto-On 12vTrigger RackMountReady HighLevelInputs AMP 50 25 30 NA 2 2 AMP 100","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41Zp+H2mKTL._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Audiosource","source_asin":"B0013D1YLM","category_path":"Electronics"},"sku":"BM-1187527","productType":"Electronics","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0013D1YLM","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"electronics-range.jsonl","source_asin":"B0013D1YLM","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
